# Bot chat

Bot chat keeps requests, progress, decisions, and delivered files in one ongoing conversation. The same tools are available from the local and Remote Dashboards, with phone-friendly views for todos and supporting panels.

## Keep decisions moving with todos

Mark any user or Bot message as a todo from its message menu. When the Bot needs an answer before it can continue, it can mark its question as a todo for you.

Open **Todo** in the chat side panel to see pending and recently resolved items. On a phone, open the **Todo** tab to see todos across Bots.

You can finish a todo in three ways:

- choose **Reply** from the todo and send your answer; the quoted reply closes it automatically;
- choose **Mark done** when no written answer is needed;
- let the Bot close it after the matter is resolved.

Choose **Reopen** on a resolved item when it needs more work.

## Reply and quote precisely

Open a message's menu and choose **Reply** to quote the whole message. For one attachment, choose **Quote file** or **Quote image**. To quote only part of a message, select the text and choose **Quote selection**. On a phone, press and hold the message to open its actions.

The quote appears above the composer. Add your message and send it; select **×** to remove the quote. Clicking a quote in sent chat jumps to the original message, including older history.

## Follow related-message context

The Bot links replies that continue an earlier topic. From a message menu, choose **View context** to see its quoted and linked messages as a chain. Select **Show** on an item to locate it in chat. This is useful when several tasks are active in the same conversation.

## Search the conversation

Open **Search** from the chat side panel or phone menu. Search all messages from you and the Bot, or filter for **Files** or **Images**. Select a result to return to that point in the conversation.

## Open attachments and previews

Files delivered by the Bot appear as attachment cards with names, types, and sizes. Images display inline and open in an image viewer. Text and code files open in Preview; other files can be downloaded. A multi-file card also offers **Download all**.

Use **Quote file** or **Quote image** when your next instruction concerns one attachment. Files are read from the device when opened or downloaded, so keep delivered artifacts at their reported paths.

## Use Files, Git, and Preview

On desktop, the side panel keeps supporting material beside the chat:

- **Files** lists files you recently opened from this Bot conversation.
- **Git** shows changes and commit history for a Workspace you choose.
- **Preview** opens supported attachments, source files, images, and structured data without leaving the chat.

On a phone, choose **Files** or **Git** from the Bot menu; file previews open as their own screen.

See [Bots](/docs/bots) for setup and settings, or [Helpers](/docs/bots/helpers) for parallel delegation.
